    Remove deprecated HUB support (#4971)
    
    ### Description
    
    Remove the deprecated FL HUB feature and its remaining runtime,
    documentation, and test surface.
    
    - Delete the `nvflare.app_common.hub` implementation and component
    registry entries.
    - Remove the HUB-only `from_hub_site` metadata and
    signature-verification exceptions so deployments follow the normal
    signed-job policy.
    - Remove HUB-specific tests, the deprecated guide and diagram, and
    current design notes.
    - Preserve historical release notes unchanged.
    
    This PR is intentionally limited to HUB removal. The
    Launcher/Cell/FilePipe refactor and third-party cleanup will be handled
    separately.
    
    ### User impact
    
    Configurations that still reference the deprecated HUB components must
    stop using them. Non-HUB jobs continue through the existing deployment
    path, with standard signature verification applied consistently.
    
    ### Validation
    
    - 116 focused unit tests passed against current `main`.
    - Black, isort, and Flake8 passed for affected Python files.
    - Component registry JSON and `git diff --check` passed.
    - Sphinx dummy documentation build passed.
    
    ### Types of changes
    
    - [ ] Non-breaking change (fix or new feature that would not break
    existing functionality).
    - [x] Breaking change (removes deprecated functionality).
    - [ ] New tests added to cover the changes.
    - [ ] Quick tests passed locally by running `./runtest.sh`.
    - [ ] In-line docstrings updated.
    - [x] Documentation updated.
    
